= Constant-product market maker =

== Overview ==
'''Constant-product market maker''' is an automated market maker whose basic two-asset reserve rule maintains a product relation of the form x·y=k, subject to fees and implementation details.

If a trader removes some amount of one reserve, the mechanism requires enough of the other reserve to move the state along the constant-product curve. This produces a continuously changing marginal price as reserve ratios change.

The formula supplies liquidity over a very broad price range but causes larger trades to move farther along the curve, creating greater price impact when reserves are shallow relative to trade size.

Real implementations include fees, discrete arithmetic, protocol constraints, and sometimes time-weighted or concentrated-liquidity extensions, so the simple equation is a model of the core mechanism rather than every accounting detail.

== Boundaries ==
* constant-product market maker ≠ every AMM
* x·y=k model ≠ zero price impact
* invariant ≠ fixed market price

